        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(release): preserve emoji in ClawHub error details",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where release operators could receive malformed ClawHub error details when an external response placed an emoji across the 400 UTF-16-unit diagnostic limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe release path now reuses the repository's surrogate-safe truncation helper while preserving the existing limit and suffix. Focused tests cover both a pair split by the boundary and a complete pair ending at the boundary.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the source-to-error path and the shared helper contract.\n\n## User Impact\n\nClawHub release diagnostics remain valid Unicode when external error bodies contain emoji. ASCII behavior and the existing diagnostic length policy are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: a 399-character prefix followed by an emoji leaves trailing UTF-16 code unit `0xd83d` after `String.slice(0, 400)`.\n- Added focused coverage in `test/plugin-clawhub-release.test.ts` for split and complete surrogate-pair boundaries through the retry/error path.\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check scripts/lib/plugin-clawhub-release.ts test/plugin-clawhub-release.test.ts`\n- Exact-head CI run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29404173183: `check-lint` passed and `test/plugin-clawhub-release.test.ts` passed 55 tests in `checks-node-compact-small-7`.\n- The run's remaining failures are in untouched current-main surfaces: agent delegate test types, gateway method registration, state DB transaction isolation, and agent harness selection.\n",
        "branch": "fix/clawhub-error-utf16-safe-20260715",
